The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the API allows users to access resources based on user-supplied identifiers (in this case, the `imageId` in the URL) without proper authorization checks. If the application does not verify whether the requesting user has permission to access the specified resource, an attacker could manipulate the `imageId` parameter to access or share images that they do not own or are not authorized to view. This lack of access control can lead to unauthorized exposure of sensitive data or resources.

